# toy-os -- a scripted tour, for showing the system without typing.
#
# Runs only when `demo` is on the kernel command line (`make demo-iso`).
# Format and verbs: apps/demo.h. Editing this file changes the tour --
# it is read off the filesystem at boot, so no rebuild is needed if you
# are editing it on a live image.
#
# Timings assume somebody is reading the screen, not a machine parsing
# it. They are the main thing worth adjusting.

say Welcome to toy-os
wait 1500

say What is this thing?
sh about
wait 4000

say What is it running on?
sh lscpu
wait 4000

# The point of the live image: this filesystem came off the CD, not a
# disk, and `df` says so itself rather than us claiming it.
say Where is the filesystem?
sh df
wait 4000

say What ships with it?
sh ls /bin/wm/apps
wait 2500
sh ls /usr/wm/desktop
wait 3000

# A real integrity check over the volume that was just mounted from RAM.
say Is the filesystem sound?
sh fsck
wait 4000

say Starting the desktop
wait 1500
gui

# From here every step is performed from inside the window manager's
# loop, one per frame, through the same path the GUI test tools use.
wait 2000
open About
wait 3500

open Calculator
wait 3000

open Notepad
wait 3000

# Shapes last, switched to its 3D scene: a perspective-projected
# wireframe cube, drawn with the kernel's own fixed-point geometry code
# (there is no floating point in this kernel at all).
open Shapes
wait 3000
key 0x73
wait 1000
end
